    <statement><p>Simplify the rational expression
<me>\frac{1}{x^{4}} + \frac{1}{x^{6}}</me>
in the form <m>\frac{A}{B}</m>.  Express the final result in a single fraction using positive exponents only.</p>
<p>Answer: <m>A =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/> and <m>B =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>x^{2}+1</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>x^{4+2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
